es":[{"pos":28533,"endPos":28594,"startLine":637,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":637,"endLineOffset":73,"length":62}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContext.java--2120:2205,2414:2425,2841:2858","promptId":"#SR6T4","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContext.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2120,"endPos":2205,"startLine":44,"startLineOffset":7,"endLine":44,"endLineOffset":92,"length":86},{"pos":2414,"endPos":2425,"startLine":51,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":51,"endLineOffset":19,"length":12},{"pos":2841,"endPos":2858,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":71,"endLineOffset":25,"length":18}]}]},{"comment":"Removing the overridden method `getMetadataMappers()` from `XPackPlugin` might break functionality if other parts of the code rely on this method being present. Verify that no other part of the codebase depends on this specific implementation and consider deprecating or providing an alternative if necessary.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/XPackPlugin.java-x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/XPackPlugin.java-14500:14670-","promptId":"#FA9ZT","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/XPackPlugin.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/XPackPlugin.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":14500,"endPos":14670,"startLine":306,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":309,"endLineOffset":5,"length":171}],"dstChanges":[]}]},{"comment":"The method `tierFieldTermQueryCoordinatorRewriteIfPresent` is quite long and does multiple things. It would be beneficial to break it down into smaller, more focused methods for better readability and maintainability. Additionally, the use of `assert false` can be problematic in production code as assertions are often disabled. Consider throwing an exception or logging an error instead.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/AbstractQueryBuilder.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/AbstractQueryBuilder.java--12810:14934","promptId":"#8G8MY","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/AbstractQueryBuilder.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/AbstractQueryBuilder.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":12810,"endPos":14934,"startLine":335,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":374,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2125}]}]},{"comment":"The method name `indexRandomDocs` is used but not defined within the provided context. This could lead to a compilation error unless this method is defined elsewhere in the class or imported from another class.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java-x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java--53402:61333","promptId":"#5Z0R6","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":53402,"endPos":61333,"startLine":974,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1113,"endLineOffset":5,"length":7932}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":114,"line":162,"comment_lines":["[][162]"],"review_comment":["It seems redundant that we are returning both the tier and exposing the constant field type too. Can\u0027t we get the current tier from the artificial data tier field type?","I believe we need the `tier` as the `CoordinatorRewriteContext` doesn\u0027t know of `indexSettings` otherwise https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/114990/files/67f82e9aa742e223de4cd6a76d496ac66987130e#diff-45c9ed5af87237215a5a11f3d2549aa678272c2cbc898b866b43516ec992fab5R60\r\nThe index settings would be needed for us to parse the `_tier_preference` setting.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m not sure if it should ? Or if we should keep just passing the `tier` ? It _seems_ that passing the tier is a smaller change (easier to test too). ","I was under the impression that that is the same value that the constant field type that the context exposes returns, or is that something else?","The field type does not store any state but every time it evaluates it reaches out to the index settings for the `_tier_preference` value https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/114990/files/67f82e9aa742e223de4cd6a76d496ac66987130e#diff-e776fbfb85ffa7c76ad9fbbd1263953047589070bf15add46298deaf929778dbR95\r\n\r\nThe `QueryWriteContext` stores the index settings (but the `CoordinatorRewriteContext` doesn\u0027t)","sounds good, I had misunderstood."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContext.java","id":35576,"created_at":"2024-10-21T10:56:11Z","original_position":63,"side":"RIGHT","position":123,"submitted_on_commit":"67f82e9aa742e223de4cd6a76d496ac66987130e","diff_hunk":"@@ -99,4 +108,8 @@ public IndexLongFieldRange getFieldRange(String fieldName) {\n     public CoordinatorRewriteContext convertToCoordinatorRewriteContext() {\n         return this;\n     }\n+\n+    public String tier() {\n+        return tier;\n+    }","submitted_line":114},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":31,"uncoveredMatchable":7,"timing":131126,"tokensIn":31531,"tokensOut":1667}